# First sheet -- proving the harness on four programs of different shapes:
# print-and-stop, a prompt-driven one, a curses one, and a shell pipeline.
shot    today
cap     Prints the date, the time and the phase of the moon in words.
run     /dd/CMDS/today
wait    3

shot    textb
cap     The Mandelbrot set, drawn in ASCII on an 80x24 terminal.  It asks for
cap     a centre and a range; -2.3, -2.0, 4.0 gives the whole set.
run     /dd/CMDS/textb
wait    2
send    -2.3\r
wait    1
send    -2.0\r
wait    1
send    4.0\r
wait    25

shot    queens
cap     The eight-queens problem, solved and drawn.  An IOCCC entry: it reads
cap     the board size on standard input.
run     /dd/CMDS/queens
wait    1
send    8\r
wait    6

shot    banner-demo
cap     banner, the letters made of their own initials.
run     /dd/CMDS/banner OS-9
wait    3
